# Normalize all text files to LF line endings on checkout, regardless of
# each contributor's local core.autocrlf setting.
#
# WHY IT IS HERE. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# source file to CRLF, and scripts/build.js matches its anchors EXACTLY —
# patch() throws unless its find matches once. A line ending is invisible in
# a diff and fatal to an anchor, so the failure arrives eighty steps into a
# build somebody waited half an hour for, saying nothing about line endings.
# That happened once. Nothing in the repository was CRLF when this landed, so
# it changes no existing file; it only stops the next one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are DECLARED, not detected. git's auto-detection reads the
# first few KB for NUL bytes and gets these right today — checked by cloning
# the repo and comparing hashes, all identical — but a file whose header
# happens to look textual would be normalized and silently corrupted, and a
# corrupted font or image is not something a test suite would catch.
*.woff2 binary
*.webp binary
